<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Raspopovic et al. (2014) 3-node Bmp-Sox9-Wnt Turing digit patterning network modulated by distal FGF on a moving-boundary FEM limb-bud outgrowth mesh (Embryonic mouse autopod (Mus musculus, E11.5-E13.5))",
        "Raspopovic et al. (2014) 3-node Bmp-Sox9-Wnt Turing digit patterning network modulated by distal FGF on a moving-boundary FEM limb-bud outgrowth mesh faithfully reproduces Embryonic mouse autopod (Mus musculus, E11.5-E13.5) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-6> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Embryonic mouse autopod (Mus musculus, E11.5-E13.5) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 84.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py> ;
    schema:about "Embryonic mouse autopod (Mus musculus, E11.5-E13.5)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A reproduction of the Raspopovic et al. (2014) supplementary growing-domain simulations, measured outgrowth kinetics of the mouse limb bud, the posterior-to-anterior order of digit condensation (the model inserts new rays in the interior), chondrogenic condensation mechanics, 3D geometry, or digit identity",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 3-node and reduced 2-diffuser Jacobians, dispersion relation and D = 0 control (Laws 1-3); 1D distal-arc explicit solver; 2D polar-fan finite-difference solver carried from v2; 7-regime FGF/Hox table; 6-condition perturbation suite; DoG + chromogen segmentation of the WISH specimen (5 WT vs 6 Tbx2-/- rays)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: P1 finite-element solver on a Lagrangian / ALE polar-fan mesh with a moving AER boundary, implicit diffusion, conservative lumped-mass dilution, re-assembled stiffness, AER-anchored wavelength modulation with three modes, FEM verification against the analytic dispersion relation, growth-dilution sweep, final-arc sweep, 3 x 3 modulation ablation, 9 new reference-anchored measurements and 3 new Lean theorems (Laws 4-6)",
        "reported_in_source: Boehm et al. (2010): finite-element limb-bud growth; a proliferation gradient alone does not explain the bud shape",
        "reported_in_source: Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999): on a growing domain every species acquires the dilution term -(div u) c and modes are inserted sequentially as the domain lengthens",
        "reported_in_source: Farin et al. (2013): E12.5 Sox9 / E13.5 Col2a1 WISH of wild-type (5) and Tbx2-/- (6) digit condensations (the vendored specimen)",
        "reported_in_source: Raspopovic et al. (2014): a 3-node network of cell-autonomous Sox9 with diffusing Bmp and Wnt (Sox9 represses both ligands, Bmp activates and Wnt represses Sox9) is Turing-unstable without ligand self-activation; Sox9 digit stripes are out of phase with Bmp and Wnt; on the growing autopod a distal FGF / Hoxd gradient that lengthens the wavelength keeps the stripes unbranched, and the growing-domain simulations were run on a realistic limb-bud growth map (Marcon et al. 2011)",
        "reported_in_source: Sheth et al. (2012): digit number scales with autopod width / Hox dosage through the Turing wavelength",
        "reported_in_source: Shubin & Alberch (1986): the digital arch forms posterior to anterior with the marginal digit I last",
        "transfer_boundary: All new reference values are analytic consequences of the baseline parameters (dispersion relation, Lean Laws 4-6) or qualitative statements from the papers; no digitised stripe count, growth curve or width-vs-digit-number data are vendored",
        "transfer_boundary: The FGF / Hoxd modulation enters as D ∝ (r / R(t))^2 (lambda ∝ r / R(t)); this is the unique modulation that keeps sigma_max fixed while scaling lambda with the arc, not an equation of Raspopovic et al. (2014), whose supplementary modulation functions were not retrieved",
        "transfer_boundary: The mesh is a prescribed polar fan (r_prox = 4.2, R: 5.0 -> 8.4, theta_max = 0.38 pi) with a uniform radial Lagrangian stretch and an exponential-then-capped outgrowth law; there is no proliferation field, no realistic bud outline, no dorsoventral axis and no measured growth kinetics",
        "transfer_boundary: The v2 7-regime FGF/Hox collapse depends on a fitted exponent (3.12) in a diffusion scaling that the network itself does not produce; the v2 LDN / CHIR digit counts are capped by hand; the v2 2D polar-fan result is mode-seeded and cosmetically masked (all three are disclosed here and carried as Pass 4 items)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "2. Morphogen + Condensations" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Skeletal Rays & Joints" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "French-Flag / PSHM Thresholds" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Mus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py; output: docs/media/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits_comparison.png; organism: Embryonic mouse autopod (Mus musculus, E11.5-E13.5); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: fcc019aeaf38ae13b447dccbc8f276f80745d761e03ea95627ecad0617dd1321; artifact_sha256: 22b27c34b46a015ca80913991f77bbaec823119454402539c53eb86847740d91; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits_reference.json=c0444b665610be2e..., datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/limb_bud_outgrowth_fem_reference.json=3db7c9493f12c2b3..., datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/paper_citations.bib=88ff32a60b567060..., datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/paper_citations_pass3.bib=eab1e111424c9ac1..., datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/scout_manifest.json=f990b473b6a93cfa..., datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/sox9_limb_digits_specimen.jpg=533f621904d6f2ce...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Raspopovic et al. (2014): a 3-node network of cell-autonomous Sox9 with diffusing Bmp and Wnt (Sox9 represses both ligands, Bmp activates and Wnt represses Sox9) is Turing-unstable without ligand self-activation; Sox9 digit stripes are out of phase with Bmp and Wnt; on the growing autopod a distal FGF / Hoxd gradient that lengthens the wavelength keeps the stripes unbranched, and the growing-domain simulations were run on a realistic limb-bud growth map (Marcon et al. 2011) | Sheth et al. (2012): digit number scales with autopod width / Hox dosage through the Turing wavelength | Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999): on a growing domain every species acquires the dilution term -(div u) c and modes are inserted sequentially as the domain lengthens | Boehm et al. (2010): finite-element limb-bud growth; a proliferation gradient alone does not explain the bud shape | Farin et al. (2013): E12.5 Sox9 / E13.5 Col2a1 WISH of wild-type (5) and Tbx2-/- (6) digit condensations (the vendored specimen) | Shubin & Alberch (1986): the digital arch forms posterior to anterior with the marginal digit I last; reconstructed_in_script: 3-node and reduced 2-diffuser Jacobians, dispersion relation and D = 0 control (Laws 1-3); 1D distal-arc explicit solver; 2D polar-fan finite-difference solver carried from v2; 7-regime FGF/Hox table; 6-condition perturbation suite; DoG + chromogen segmentation of the WISH specimen (5 WT vs 6 Tbx2-/- rays) | Pass 3: P1 finite-element solver on a Lagrangian / ALE polar-fan mesh with a moving AER boundary, implicit diffusion, conservative lumped-mass dilution, re-assembled stiffness, AER-anchored wavelength modulation with three modes, FEM verification against the analytic dispersion relation, growth-dilution sweep, final-arc sweep, 3 x 3 modulation ablation, 9 new reference-anchored measurements and 3 new Lean theorems (Laws 4-6); transfer_boundary: The mesh is a prescribed polar fan (r_prox = 4.2, R: 5.0 -> 8.4, theta_max = 0.38 pi) with a uniform radial Lagrangian stretch and an exponential-then-capped outgrowth law; there is no proliferation field, no realistic bud outline, no dorsoventral axis and no measured growth kinetics | The FGF / Hoxd modulation enters as D ∝ (r / R(t))^2 (lambda ∝ r / R(t)); this is the unique modulation that keeps sigma_max fixed while scaling lambda with the arc, not an equation of Raspopovic et al. (2014), whose supplementary modulation functions were not retrieved | All new reference values are analytic consequences of the baseline parameters (dispersion relation, Lean Laws 4-6) or qualitative statements from the papers; no digitised stripe count, growth curve or width-vs-digit-number data are vendored | The v2 7-regime FGF/Hox collapse depends on a fitted exponent (3.12) in a diffusion scaling that the network itself does not produce; the v2 LDN / CHIR digit counts are capped by hand; the v2 2D polar-fan result is mode-seeded and cosmetically masked (all three are disclosed here and carried as Pass 4 items); does_not_claim: A reproduction of the Raspopovic et al. (2014) supplementary growing-domain simulations, measured outgrowth kinetics of the mouse limb bud, the posterior-to-anterior order of digit condensation (the model inserts new rays in the interior), chondrogenic condensation mechanics, 3D geometry, or digit identity]" ;
