<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raspopovic et al. (2014) 3-node Bmp-Sox9-Wnt Turing digit patterning network modulated by distal FGF on a moving-boundary FEM limb-bud outgrowth mesh — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring maps each solver and each of the 6 Lean laws to its source (L1-104); the Section 3b header states geometry, growth law, boundary condition and length unit (L669-679); `simulate_growing_limb_bud_fem` documents the scheme, the three modulation modes and the reduction (L798-818); the registry YAML pins Lean and code loci for laws 4-6 (morphoeval/math_kg_loops/raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.yaml L86-135). Deductions: the exponent 3.12 (L318), the per-condition basal offsets and caps (L617-629, L644-649), the envelope constants 0.45 / 0.35 / 0.0008 of the v2 fan (L511-514, L549) and the ray-count threshold 0.35 (L754) have no citation (-8); the F -> D mapping is justified by an invariance argument rather than by a paper equation (-4); the arc sweep's expected counts use lambda = 4 while the script's lambda_c is 4.002 (stated, but a second convention) (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py L617–L629: Hand-set basal Sox9 offsets and IWP-2 parameter overrides without citation (deduction) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py#L617-L629>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raspopovic et al. (2014) 3-node Bmp-Sox9-Wnt Turing digit patterning network modulated by distal FGF on a moving-boundary FEM limb-bud outgrowth mesh — Model fidelity to source: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The core of the paper is implemented correctly and now exercised on a growing domain: exact 3-node and reduced Jacobians and dispersion relation (L206-301, Lean Laws 1-3), a P1 FEM whose stiffness reproduces the Laplacian of x^2 to 4e-16 and whose seeded-mode growth rate is within 2.2 % of Re sigma(q_c) (L960-1030), a conservative ALE update that is the exact discrete form of the Crampin-Gaffney-Maini dilution term (L883-886, Lean Law 4), implicit diffusion with re-assembly on the moving mesh (L874-876), and unbiased-noise initial conditions (L845-848). Deductions: the v2 2D polar-fan solver that still feeds one measurement seeds the target 5-ray mode (L526-528), scales radial diffusion by 0.0008 (L549-550) and masks the output with a cosmetic envelope (L514, L560-567), so its '5 radial digits' are imposed (-6); the 7-regime FGF/Hox collapse uses a fitted diffusion exponent 3.12 (L318) although the network's own dispersion relation shortens lambda_c when k_bs rises (5.02 -> 3.27 for k_bs 1.0 -> 3.2), i.e. the table is fitted, not predicted (-5); the FEM wavelength modulation D ∝ (r/R(t))^2 (L850-856) is a modelling choice, not the paper's modulation function (-3); the fan geometry, uniform stretch and exponential-capped outgrowth (L712-718, L871) replace the paper's realistic growth map (-2); the perturbation suite applies hand-set basal Sox9 offsets per condition (L617-629) (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py L318–L318: Fitted diffusion scaling exponent 3.12 that manufactures the FGF/Hox wavelength collapse (deduction) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py#L318-L318>",
        "2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py L526–L528: v2 2D fan solver seeds the target angular mode as its initial condition (deduction) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py#L526-L528>",
        "2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py L850–L856: D ∝ (r/R(t))^2 modulation: declared reduction, not the paper's modulation function (deduction) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py#L850-L856>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raspopovic et al. (2014) 3-node Bmp-Sox9-Wnt Turing digit patterning network modulated by distal FGF on a moving-boundary FEM limb-bud outgrowth mesh — Morphometric validation: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1698-1905) returns 18 measurements: the 9 v2 metrics plus 9 Pass 3 metrics with `reference_value`, `reference_source` and units — FEM ray count 5/5, bifurcation range 0/0, sigma_FEM error 0.022/0, ALE mass error 0/0, dilution slope -1.000/-1, rho_c 0.265/0.261, arc slope 0.225/0.250, addition events 3/2, marginal-insertion fraction 0.00/1.00 (L1721-1812). Deductions: eight of the nine new references are analytic or model-internal (dispersion relation, Lean laws) or qualitative statements, not measured values (-8); the one specimen-anchored qualitative reference (marginal digits last) is NOT met and the addition-event count overshoots its analytic reference (3 vs 2), both reported honestly (-3); the specimen metrics are still not compared with the FEM output (-4); the v2 '2D fan count = 5' measurement remains in the list although it is mode-seeded (-3)." ;
